  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Opportunities for Dutch-Colombian Cooperation on Circular Economy 2022-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this study is to identify the best ways for the Netherlands and Colombia to collaborate on Circular Economy in priority areas such as agriculture, water, mobility, waste, and renewable energy. This project&apos;s outcomes will help to monitor the progress of the implementation of Colombia&apos;s National Strategy for Circular Economy 2022-2026 and define specific opportunities for bilateral cooperation in priority sectors of the embassy, with a focus on areas where the Netherlands can offer additional support to promote sustainable local economic growth.This initiative will foster valuable partnerships between the public and private sectors and create synergies with international organizations to develop circular solutions in Colombia. By doing so, the project will also pinpoint opportunities for the involvement of Dutch and Colombian private sectors&apos; knowledge and innovation.Overall, this project seeks to identify alternatives for sustainable development of the local private sector, which will contribute to promoting sustainable economic growth in Colombia.</narrative>
  </description>
